Developer Workflow
Version: 2026-07-23
Status: Authoritative Developer Guide

Overview
This document explains how to work on the WordList Writer codebase. It merges the original developer workflow with updated Phase 2 architecture rules, tokenizer rules, rendering rules, highlight pipeline rules, startup sequence rules, hybrid master list model, and July 19 fixes. All Phase 3 dictionary profile, alphabetical dictionary, merged dictionary, and cognate publishing features have been removed. It is designed for future developers and future sessions that need to reconstruct the internal architecture, pipelines, and coding conventions. It follows the GitHub-safe formatting rules used across the project.

Architecture Overview
WordList Writer consists of four major layers:
* UI Layer (HTML, CSS, JS)
* Analysis Layer (tokenizer, normalization, highlight pipeline)
* Curriculum Layer (Master List, Project List, Cognates, Frequency)
* Backend Layer (Express plus Supabase)
The system uses static JSON files for linguistic data, a lightweight Express server, and Supabase for persistence. WordList Writer is a teacher-facing authoring tool.

