SaveEverything Workflow
SaveEverything must:
Step 1: save project metadata
Step 2: capture returned id
Step 3: save project wordlist
Step 4: save master list
Step 5: update UI
Rules:
* project-id-input must always be updated
* masterList must be saved as plain strings
* Supabase rows must be { project_id, lemma }
This order must never change.

Load Workflow
Load workflow must:
Step 1: load project metadata
Step 2: load project wordlist
Step 3: load master list
Step 4: rebuild UI state
Step 5: trigger highlight via requestHighlightUpdate
Rules:
* project-id-input must be updated
* master list must render after assignment

Updated Architecture Rules
Centralized Highlight Pipeline:
* all highlight operations must enter through requestHighlightUpdate
* requestHighlightUpdate uses debounce
* no other function may trigger highlight
IME Rules:
* no highlight during composition
Startup Rules:
* startup triggers highlight once
* project list and order check run after highlight
* recommended delay is 75ms
Frequency Rules:
* frequencySet must contain normalized lemmas
* known words come from NGSL-1K
Debug Logging Rules:
* no normalized token logs
* no lemmaMap prefix logs
* no sample frequency logs
* only "Load complete" allowed on startup

Debugging Workflow
Common debugging steps:
* check normalizeLemma
* check tokenizer output
* check masterSet
* check frequencySet
* check detectCognates
* check highlight pipeline
* check violations panel
* check save and load pipeline
* check for nested spans in editor.innerHTML
* check project-id-input for correct value

Adding New Features
When adding new features:
* update Decisions.md
* update Detailed_Feature_Specifications.md
* update API_Specification.md if backend changes
* update Supabase_Schema.md if schema changes
* update README.md if user-facing changes
* update Docs_Index.md
Rules:
* never modify masterList directly; use helper functions
* always normalize lemmas before insertion
* always update masterSet after changes
* always trigger highlight via requestHighlightUpdate
* always validate ranks
* always guard against null values

Summary
This developer workflow explains how to work on the WordList Writer codebase, how pipelines interact, how the backend integrates with Supabase, and how to safely add new features. It reflects correct Phase 2 behavior: English-only master list, simple cognate window, stable tokenizer behavior, and predictable highlight operations. All Phase 3 cognate dictionary architecture has been removed to maintain stability.

